course: dictionary
lesson: 10330
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word trailer is a good example. «A lorry's big diesel engine pulls a heavy trailer, and lots of wheels spread the weight.» Here a trailer is a wheeled box pulled behind a vehicle. The words lorry, engine and wheels are your clues.
explain: Now read this: «Cinemas show adverts and trailers before the film.» Cinemas do not pull boxes behind them, so the meaning has changed. Here a trailer is a short video that shows bits of a film. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «In Texas, Josiah's family lives in a trailer (a mobile home).» The brackets are a clue too: the writer has added a simpler phrase to help you. Writers do this to save you a trip to the dictionary. When there is no clue like this, use the other words around the word, and check a dictionary if you are still unsure.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is a word with several senses.
fact: «Trailer» can mean a wheeled box or platform pulled behind a car, truck or tractor to carry things or animals.
fact: «Trailer» can also mean a short video that shows the most exciting bits of a film, show or game.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a «trailer» can mean a caravan or mobile home where people live or go on holiday.
exercise: «A lorry's big diesel engine pulls a heavy trailer.» What is the trailer in this sentence? | A kind of bike | A caravan where people sleep on holiday | A short video of a film | *A wheeled box pulled behind a lorry
exercise: «Cinemas show adverts and trailers before the film.» What does trailers mean here? | Long films shown in the afternoon | Wheeled boxes pulled by tractors | *Short videos showing bits of films | Homes where people live
exercise: «In Texas, Josiah's family lives in a trailer (a mobile home).» What do the brackets tell you trailer means? | A cinema seat | *A mobile home | A boat | A horse
test: «Theo's phone buzzed with his friends arguing about the GTA 6 trailer.» What is the trailer here? | A caravan in a trailer park | A wheeled box for carrying a game | *A short video that shows bits of a game | A horse box
test: «Trailers show the most exciting or scary bits squeezed together, so a trailer can feel scarier than the whole film.» What does this tell you about trailers? | They are always longer than the film | They are only shown on Sundays | *They can make a film seem scarier than it really is | They are wheeled boxes for carrying tools
exam: Which meaning of trailer fits «Josiah's family lives in a trailer»? | A tractor part | A short video of a film | A wheeled box for carrying things | *A mobile home where people live
